1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,716
My story begins in the cool mornings of
Wegeltena, Delanta.

2
00:00:09,716 --> 00:00:16,716
I studied Grades 1–4 at Wegeltena Mesno
Amba Primary School.

3
00:00:16,716 --> 00:00:23,716
When my teacher mother moved to
Kombolcha, I continued Grade 5 there.

4
00:00:23,716 --> 00:00:31,716
In Grade 7, emergency appendicitis
surgery brought me back from death.

5
00:00:31,716 --> 00:00:39,716
From Grade 8, balancing Abinet church
study and modern school side by side...

6
00:00:39,716 --> 00:00:48,304
I became a deacon in Grade 10 and
learned to manage time wisely beyond...

7
00:00:48,304 --> 00:00:56,304
At Wollo University I dreamed of
Medicine, but a connection glitch...

8
00:00:56,304 --> 00:01:04,304
I grieved then—now thriving in 3rd-year
Software Engineering, that discipline...

9
00:01:04,304 --> 00:01:12,304
Every trial and closed door was for
good—leading to a better path.

10
00:01:12,304 --> 00:01:18,588
All asked of you is to try your best;
trust the Creator with the rest.
